<control>{"schema":"deep-research-final-synthesis-v2","digest":"MCP stdio uses newline-delimited JSON-RPC; stdout is reserved for valid MCP messages, while stderr permits UTF-8 logging.","synthesis":{"bottomLine":"The current MCP specification (2026-07-28) frames stdio messages with newlines. Each message is a single JSON-RPC request, notification, or response and MUST NOT contain embedded newlines. Servers MUST NOT write anything to stdout that is not a valid MCP message. Servers MAY write UTF-8 strings to stderr for any logging purposes, including informational, debug, and error messages. Clients SHOULD NOT assume stderr output indicates an error.","comparisonRows":[],"keyFindingIds":["claim-001","claim-002","claim-003","claim-005","claim-006","claim-007","claim-008"],"recommendations":[{"recommendation":"Keep diagnostic logs and startup banners off stdout; use stderr for logging.","supportingClaimIds":["claim-006","claim-007"]}],"actionPlan":[],"caveatNotes":[{"note":"General wire-message encoding remains unestablished: slot-003 is missing, and framing scope coverage is partial despite completed research-question runs. UTF-8 permission for stderr does not establish message encoding.","readerNote":"The retrieved evidence establishes UTF-8 for stderr logging, not the encoding requirement for protocol messages.","gapIds":["gap-coverage-001","gap-coverage-002"]}],"parentDecisionNotes":[]}}</control>

<analysis>
The official [versioning page](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning) identifies 2026-07-28 as current. Its [stdio specification](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md) states: “Messages are delimited by newlines, and MUST NOT contain embedded newlines.”

The audited evidence supports the framing and stream rules above. Newline delimiting appears in verified evidence for claim-005 and the transport overview supporting claim-002; its separately preserved claim is not promoted to verified. Additional preserved claims likewise remain unverified.

All required pages were read without truncation and reconcile with the header. Verifier integrity is clean, but message-encoding coverage remains incomplete. Schema-file validation was not performed because this stage prohibits filesystem reads.
